course: dictionary
lesson: 5829
title: Main: the most important one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word main has several meanings, but they share one idea: the most important or the biggest one. In «Palermo is its main city», main means Palermo is the biggest and most important city on the island.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. In «A burst water main flooded the street», a main is a large pipe that carries water. Check by swapping in your meaning: does the sentence still make sense?
explain: In a story, the main character is the most important person. In a reading text, the main idea is what the text is mostly about. Signal words like "first" and "the most important thing" often point to it.
fact: Main means the most important or the biggest one.
fact: Main can be an adjective, as in «the main idea», or a noun, as in «a main», which is a large pipe or cable.
fact: The mains is the electricity supply from the wall sockets.
fact: Mains electricity is strong enough to kill, so never poke things into sockets.
fact: In British English, the main course is the biggest part of a meal.
exercise: «Palermo is its main city.» What does main mean here? | A pipe that carries water | The cheapest one | The smallest one | *The biggest and most important one
exercise: «A burst water main flooded the street.» What is a main in this sentence? | The most important person | A type of meal | A main road for cars | *A large pipe that carries water
exercise: In a story, what is the main character? | A small picture on the page | *The most important person in the story | The last word of the story | The name of the author
test: «Never poke things into the mains.» Why is this important? | The mains is a kind of food | Sockets are full of water | *Mains electricity is strong enough to kill | Pokes make the lights brighter
test: What is the main idea of a text? | *What the text is mostly about | The name of the publisher | The number of pages | The first word of the text
exam: In «The main course was pasta», what does main course mean? | A drink with the meal | *The biggest part of the meal | A sweet dessert | A starter before the meal
